---
/* L11 - the 0.1 + 0.2 trap: compare with a tolerance, round only for printing. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L11.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of a mechanical weighing scale with a many-marked dial and a single needle, a pair of calipers held beside the dial, and a blank sheet of paper resting on the platform above."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L11-fig-title L11-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L11-fig-title">A hair of difference, and the window that swallows it</title>
      <desc id="L11-fig-desc">
        A magnified number line carries a tick at 0.3 and, a hair to its right, a
        prussian tick at 0.30000000000000004. Both sit inside a pale band, the
        tolerance window, and a bracket closes over the gap between them. Below,
        three pairs show a value beside its four-decimal rounding:
        0.30000000000000004 becomes 0.3, 0.99995 becomes 1.0, and 0.72 against
        0.70 gives a relative error of 0.028.
      </desc>

      <!-- the tolerance window and the number line -->
      <text x="60" y="58" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">compare with a tolerance</text>
      <text x="60" y="78" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">abs(a - b) &lt; 1e-9 for probabilities, 1e-12 for sums</text>

      <rect x="150" y="111" width="200" height="28" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" />
      <text x="155" y="104" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">the window</text>
      <line x1="60" y1="125" x2="580" y2="125" class="fig-axis-line" />

      <line x1="250" y1="107" x2="250" y2="143" stroke="var(--color-ink)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="257" y1="113" x2="257" y2="137" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />

      <path
        class="m-draw"
        style="--m-length: 40; --m-duration: 1.2s;"
        d="M 246 107 L 246 99 L 264 99 L 264 107"
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--color-prussian)"
        stroke-width="1"
      />
      <text x="255" y="92" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">the gap</text>

      <text x="250" y="158" class="fig-text fig-text--num fig-text--ink" text-anchor="middle">0.3</text>
      <text x="268" y="158" class="fig-text fig-text--num" fill="var(--color-prussian)">0.30000000000000004</text>
      <text x="400" y="129" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">magnified</text>

      <!-- rounding is for printing -->
      <text x="60" y="196" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">round for printing, never for deciding</text>

      <defs>
        <marker id="L11-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="var(--color-ink-45)" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <text x="60" y="226" class="fig-text fig-text--num fig-text--dim">0.30000000000000004</text>
      <path d="M 96 234 L 96 252" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L11-arrow)" />
      <text x="96" y="270" class="fig-text fig-text--num fig-text--ink" text-anchor="middle">0.3</text>
      <text x="60" y="292" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">round to 4 places</text>
      <text x="60" y="308" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">printing only</text>

      <text x="230" y="226" class="fig-text fig-text--num fig-text--dim">0.99995</text>
      <path d="M 266 234 L 266 252" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L11-arrow)" />
      <text x="266" y="270" class="fig-text fig-text--num fig-text--ink" text-anchor="middle">1.0</text>
      <text x="230" y="292" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">an option can vanish</text>

      <text x="420" y="226" class="fig-text fig-text--num fig-text--dim">0.72 vs 0.70</text>
      <path d="M 456 234 L 456 252" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L11-arrow)" />
      <text x="456" y="270" class="fig-text fig-text--num fig-text--ink" text-anchor="middle">0.028</text>
      <text x="420" y="292" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">relative error</text>
      <text x="420" y="308" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">|a-b| / max(|a|,|b|)</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L11</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">A hair of difference separates 0.3 from 0.30000000000000004, and it sits well inside the tolerance window, so the comparison survives it while the rounding is kept for printing.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig-text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--color-ink-70);
  }

  .fig-text--ink {
    fill: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-text--dim {
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
    font-size: 10px;
  }

  .fig-text--num {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .fig-axis-line {
    stroke: var(--color-rule);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
</style>
